# Party banter: after the staff, Maewyn's ravens will only perch facing
# the barrow, and she and Wren draw different conclusions from it.
dialogue TSC_Banter_StaffRavens

== start ==
_You overhear Wren and Maewyn watching the ravens, who are watching the east._

Wren: They've been like that since the hall. Both of them. Like weather vanes.

Maewyn: Aye.

Wren: Corvus won't even take bread if I stand west of him. I have never in my life been refused food by an animal.

Maewyn: They sit facing the thing that is realest to them. Usually that is food. Sometimes weather.

Wren: And now it is the barrow. That is going in a song, and it is going to be a frightening song.

Maewyn: Good. Songs should tell the truth. The truth is east, and even the birds know it.

* [Leave them to it.] -> end
